{
 "_FLOW": "FIXED DOI PANEL — the Platform Erosion Observatory's global erasure instrument, and the correction to the cohort census. A COHORT COUNT MEASURES NET CHANGE: minting minus erasure. In a growing cohort, erasure is invisible unless it exceeds minting. A FIXED PANEL measures erasure directly: re-query the same DOIs each epoch and count the ones that stopped resolving. The 404 rate IS the erasure rate, and minting cannot mask it.",
 "epoch": "2026-08-23",
 "instrument": "fixed-panel survival study",
 "validation": {
  "test": "20 DOIs known to have been severed on 2026-06-19, drawn from the archive's own kill ledger, re-queried at api.datacite.org/dois/<doi> on 2026-08-23.",
  "result": "20 of 20 returned HTTP 404. Severed DOIs leave the DataCite index entirely.",
  "conclusion": "Erasure of this class is detectable by absence, which is what makes a panel work. It is NOT detectable in cohort totals — see detection_floor."
 },
 "detection_floor": {
  "cha_event": 1136,
  "cohort_2025": 34506849,
  "cohort_2026": 22385020,
  "share": "0.003% and 0.005% of those cohorts",
  "finding": "The cohort census cannot see an event of 1,136 DOIs. Worse, cohorts grow: a cohort's net change is mints minus erasures, so erasure is masked unless it dominates minting. THE COHORT CENSUS DETECTS MASS EROSION ONLY, and this limitation was not stated when it was built this morning. It is stated now."
 },
 "panel_design": {
  "size": 720,
  "cohorts": [
   "2015",
   "2018",
   "2020",
   "2022",
   "2024",
   "2025"
  ],
  "per_cohort": 120,
  "selection": "First N by created date within each publicationYear cohort, via the public API. NOT A RANDOM SAMPLE — the API's cursor ordering is by creation, so this panel is biased toward early-created DOIs within each year. A random panel would require a sampling frame the public API does not provide. THE BIAS IS DECLARED AND THE PANEL IS STILL INFORMATIVE, because survival is measured within the panel over time rather than extrapolated to the population.",
  "method_per_epoch": "GET api.datacite.org/dois/<doi> for each panel member. 200 = alive. 404 = erased. Any other code = indeterminate and recorded as such, never as erasure.",
  "cost": "720 calls per epoch"
 },
 "baseline_status": "ALL PANEL MEMBERS ALIVE AT DRAW — they were returned by the index at 2026-08-23 and are therefore findable by construction. The first meaningful measurement is the next epoch.",
 "next_epoch_due": "2026-09-23",
 "what_this_cannot_do": [
  "Estimate a global erasure rate. The panel is not a random sample and 720 DOIs cannot support a population estimate.",
  "Distinguish deletion from withdrawal-from-findability. Both produce 404 at this endpoint.",
  "Detect erasure of DOIs minted after the panel was drawn."
 ],
